course: dictionary
lesson: 7631
title: Words that announce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Proclaim means to announce something loudly and publicly, so that everyone knows. «The king proclaimed a holiday.» The king is not whispering to one person. The whole kingdom is meant to hear it.
explain: Proclaim can also mean to say something proudly or strongly. «She proclaimed she was the best speller.» Look at the clues: she is telling everyone, and she is proud. If you swap in said, the sentence still works, but you lose the strength the author chose.
explain: Historians use proclaim for official announcements. «On 22 January 1918 the Central Rada proclaimed full independence.» Here it means a government officially declared something important. Always test your meaning in the sentence: does announced publicly fit?
fact: Proclaim means to announce something officially and publicly.
fact: Proclaim can also mean to say something proudly or strongly, or to show something clearly: «His smile proclaimed his joy.»
fact: «Proclaimed» is the past tense of proclaim, and «proclaiming» is the -ing form.
fact: In church, to proclaim means to announce or preach a message, like the good news.
fact: Words like announce and declare are close in meaning to proclaim, but proclaim often sounds more formal and grand.
exercise: «The king proclaimed a holiday for the whole kingdom.» What does proclaimed mean here? | Painted on a wall | Cancelled for ever | Whispered to one friend | *Announced publicly, so everyone knows
exercise: «His smile proclaimed his joy.» What does proclaim mean in this sentence? | Asked a question | Hid | *Showed clearly | Washed away
exercise: «On 22 January 1918 the Central Rada proclaimed full independence.» Find and copy the word that shows this happened in the past. | the | *proclaimed | Rada | January
test: «The Central Rada in Kyiv proclaimed the Ukrainian People's Republic in November 1917.» What does proclaimed mean here? | *Officially announced | Forgot about | Lost track of | Asked for help with
test: A preacher stands up and proclaims the good news. What does proclaims mean in this church sense? | Asks people to guess | Writes a letter to a friend | Hides the message | *Announces the message to everyone
exam: Which sentence uses proclaim to mean show clearly? | The bell rang at noon | *Her bright red cheeks proclaimed that she had been running | He walked slowly to school | The dog slept under the table
